# Stem hints, hint masks and counter masks. A mask is as many bytes as eight
# stems take (rounded up); each probe's mask bytes are 0x15, an rmoveto
# without operands, so a mask byte read as an operator fails the glyph, and a
# byte too many swallows the first byte of the rmoveto after it.
# Every glyph ends with `100 100 rmoveto 10 20 rlineto`.
glyph
  endchar
end
glyph # 1: hstem, even: no width
  10 20 hstem 100 100 rmoveto 10 20 rlineto endchar
end
glyph # 2: hstem, odd: the first is the width
  5 10 20 hstem 100 100 rmoveto 10 20 rlineto endchar
end
glyph # 3: vstem and hstem with odd operand counts after the first
  10 20 hstem 1 2 3 vstem 100 100 rmoveto 10 20 rlineto endchar
end
glyph # 4: 8 stems: one mask byte
  0 1 2 1 4 1 6 1 hstemhm 0 1 2 1 4 1 6 1 vstemhm hintmask byte:0x15 100 100 rmoveto 10 20 rlineto endchar
end
